From 78cbb03a82234caf4094e19ec945ff742da4d104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yami <yami@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:35:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] yami: layer rule hide-from, covers over window casts

block-out-from draws a black box over the whole surface, shadow margins
included, which looks broken for notifications and the shell's own
badges in a stream. hide-from does not draw the surface to those
targets at all.

A window screencast drew only the window, so a show-only-in cover (the
shell's privacy curtain) did not hide a window shared on its own. Such
layers are now drawn over window casts too, shifted so the part of the
cover where the window is on the monitor covers the window.
